      "bullets": [
        "Modern OpenSSH private keys use the openssh-key-v1 binary format, replacing legacy OpenSSL PEM structures with magic string headers and padded keypairs.",
        "Passphrase-protected private keys employ a custom bcrypt KDF combined with AES-256-CTR symmetric encryption to mitigate offline brute-force attacks.",
        "Public key files serialize key types (e.g., ssh-ed25519, rsa-sha2-512) and parameters using uint32 length-prefixed byte arrays in RFC 4253 wire format."
      ]
